# THE LOOP'S WORKING MEMORY lives here, and none of it is tracked.
#
# A loop that runs in a fresh context window every pass needs its continuity on
# disk rather than in a conversation. These are those files: the plan whose top
# unchecked item is the next pass's job, the facts discovered so far, the
# decisions taken and superseded, the operating manual, the last failure, and
# the harness's own record of what each pass cost.
#
# WHY IGNORED RATHER THAN TRACKED. Every one of them changes on almost every
# pass. Tracking them would put a commit's worth of churn on this branch for
# each iteration of work that has not landed yet, and would make the pull
# request that carries a rung unreadable next to the change it is actually for.
# They are also per-instance by nature: another checkout of this branch is a
# different loop with a different position in it.
#
# IGNORED DOES NOT MEAN UNREADABLE, and that distinction is the whole design.
# The pipeline already reads gitignored `.harnx/` state every run by being
# handed a path in the environment: review-engine.sh reads AI_REVIEW_HANDLED and
# AI_REVIEW_OPEN exactly that way. The same applies here. Nothing needs these
# files to be in git in order to read them; it needs to be told where they are.
#
# THE MECHANISM IS TRACKED, THE INSTANCE IS NOT. What ships, what a reviewer can
# read, and what CODEOWNERS protects is scripts/ai-review/loop-init.sh, which
# holds the canonical text of every file here as a heredoc and materialises them
# on first use. A repository harnx generates receives that script and grows its
# own loop state; it does not inherit harnx's.
#
# `*` PLUS AN EXCEPTION, not an enumeration. .harnx/.gitignore lists its two
# files by name because .harnx/ mixes tracked and untracked content. This
# directory does not: everything in it except this file is instance state, so
# the catch-all is the honest rule and an enumeration would leave a silent gap
# for the next file to fall through.
#
# The ignore lives here rather than in a root .gitignore so it moves with the
# directory and dies with it.
*
!.gitignore
